WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.710
If this goes on, it's likely both
your memories will remain jumbled

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:09.190
and Birdy's personality will be
steadily overwritten by yours,

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.990
eventually being totally erased.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.860
What the heck?!

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.490
What do you mean, Birdy will disappear?!

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.800
To put it plainly, she'll cease to exist.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.000
You could say she'll die.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.970
And you'll start a new life in that body,
with fragments of Birdy's memories...

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.480
Like hell I can do that!

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.550
Don't say hopeless stuff like that so nonchalantly!

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.880
Birdy... can't die...

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.050
It's not necessarily hopeless yet.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.690
Let me confirm something, Tsutomu.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.760
Yes?

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.430
Didn't you say that before she fell into their trap,

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.230
Birdy was acting unusually upset?

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.430
Yeah, it was like...

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.570
When I talked to her, she wouldn't really answer.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.700
Oh, right!

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.510
One of the escapees used to be in
Is... Isda... what was that name again?

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.870
Isdalta?

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.510
Yeah, that's it!

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:12.080
Birdy's been acting kind of weird
ever since she found out about that.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.790
And you dreamed about Violin?

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:18.590
Are Isdalta and Violin connected?

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.690
It's definitely a flashback effect.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.700
The body's original mind
is in a state of constriction.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.870
So it's as you suspected?

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.300
Hey, I don't understand what you're saying!

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.810
Tsutomu Senkawa, we're
going to send you on a trip.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.610
A trip?

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.880
Now's no time for that!

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.880
Your destination is Birdy's memories.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:50.650
Her consciousness is currently
trapped deep within her own memories.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:54.260
Fragments of them are flowing into
you because her consciousness,

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.760
which normally acts as a filter
for that, isn't functioning.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.830
So we'll have you vicariously
experience her memories

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.330
and objectify them as knowledge.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.440
By doing that, we'll keep the
waters from getting any muddier.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.570
Will that bring Birdy back?

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:15.450
If nothing else, we should be able to
prevent the destruction of her personality.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:22.650
Right now this is our only means
of stopping further mental fusion.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.120
You'll use a tune-up tank for the mind dive.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.420
Booting unit.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.410
Starting system idling.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:22.070
Are you sure things won't get even
more confusing if I go into her memories?

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.780
Don't worry. I've specially
adjusted the seepage program

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:30.080
to keep your consciousness
independent during the dive.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.250
We'll be monitoring everything
that happens to your consciousness,

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.950
including what you're about to experience.

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.420
We'll also be able to communicate with you.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.560
On the off chance you appear to be in danger,

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.960
we'll awaken you right away.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:55.340
You may witness even more appalling
sights than the ones in your dream.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:05:00.310
But there's no need to worry.
We'll watch over you the whole time.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.300
You must not let yourself
be agitated, understand?

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.320
Birdy! Birdy, it's morning. Wake up.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.800
Good morning, Violin.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.630
Good morning, Birdy.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.640
Hey, what's for breakfast?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:31.640
It's almost ready. You go take a shower first.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.180
Okay!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.810
Do you realize that I am Maguro-maru?!

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.110
What's this?

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.720
You're currently inside memories
from when Birdy was about ten.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:46.220
It probably feels as if you're dreaming,
but you'll soon get used to it.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.230
Oh, so this person is Violin.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.660
Huh, that's right, she's not a person...

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.800
It's been almost two years
since the terrorist hit

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.230
on Acrabal's outer administrative district.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:06:02.810
Preparations for the memorial ceremony
are underway at Central Tower.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:07.640
The whereabouts of ringleader
Christella Revi remain unknown...

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.910
If you don't hurry, you'll be late.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.890
Did you forget? Today you start...

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:20.880
Oh, that's right!

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:39.910
We'll now introduce a new friend.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:43.900
I'm Birdy Cephon Altira!
Nice to meet you, everybody!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:56.290
Oriotera Military Prep School welcomes you.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:01.560
Now take your seat. It's the
one in the back, next to Miln.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.070
All right, time to begin class.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:08.100
Open your books to page 52,
and we'll study the internal discord

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.710
within the last 100 years of the Empire.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.910
What's with that board?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.140
Huh? Oh, you mean this?

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:19.650
How about you just <i>run</i>
instead of riding that dumb thing?

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.450
You're a savage, after all.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.440
Hmph.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.660
I can't believe you fell for that old trick.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.260
Proves how stupid you are.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.600
Hey, you...

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.000
If you've got something to say...

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.900
What's going on?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.670
The Altan is being violent!

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:43.770
She got Kred!

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.270
She's scary!

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.260
Stupid savage!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:53.180
If you're like this on your first day,
it doesn't bode well for the future.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:59.760
Mr. Megius, I only admitted her
because you were her guarantor.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.160
But Principal...

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.590
I wasn't violent!

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:09.000
Even if that wasn't your intent,
that's how normal students see it.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.640
What with the Acrabal memorial
ceremony and everything,

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:16.610
everyone is nervous about Altans.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.670
I'm aware it's harsh luck for her,

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:24.480
but please strictly supervise her
to prevent indiscreet behavior.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.450
<i>Mourning a terrorist act?</i>

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.790
<i>So they weren't just picking on the new girl.</i>

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:30.690
<i>Come to think of</i> it...

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.520
Nobody discriminates
against you just for being Altan.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.900
This is your fault for
sending her to some <i>school!</i>

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:42.900
It's the lizard guy!

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:46.640
I did it so she'd learn to
be sociable with people.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.870
Ha! <i>Muscles</i> are what you need in the field!

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:52.240
Birdy, I'm going to level up
your training from now on.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.710
Think you can keep up?

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:56.080
Yes, Instructor Skeletso!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.910
See you later, Captain Megius.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:06.560
Today you'll be facing ten Shio Ils
whose programming I've powered up.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.890
You'll get hurt if you're not careful.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:10.090
Tuto!

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.330
Tuto!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.700
Collect data as usual. Don't give her any advice!

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.600
I know.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.870
Good afternoon, Tuto.
Glad to work with you again.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.540
Likewise, Birdy.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.370
Okay!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:28.370
Simulation Seven! Begin training!

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.790
This is training?!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:47.560
Hey, Mr. Megius, what's with this?!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:51.470
It's battle-conditions training
for Federation Police trainees.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.740
Trainees?

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:58.810
Birdy already wanted to be
an investigator at this age?

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.110
It's not that she "wanted" to be one.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.480
It was decided that she <i>would</i> be one.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.950
She's an lxioran, after all.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:07.140
lxioran?

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:15.490
lxiorans are a superior breed of Altan
created with ancient technology.

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:18.130
Through fine-tuning by engineers,

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:24.300
they are given sturdy physiques
and various extraordinary abilities.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:27.970
We cannot leave those with such power unchecked.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.570
Therefore, they are supervised from a young age

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:36.170
and their professions are naturally
limited to the police, the military, etc.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.950
Birdy couldn't even choose her own future?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.940
That's the nature of the lxiorans.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:45.980
"Shion Arita"

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.010
Birdy...

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:56.420
How much longer will I last?

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.600
Ow ow ow ow ow!

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.570
Oh, I'm sorry. Did I do it too hard?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:07.700
It's okay. It hurts, but I
think it might feel good, too.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:13.110
We have to be sure to care for your muscles
after you train with Instructor Skeletso.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:18.280
<i>I never knew the lxiorans had</i>
<i>to follow a preset path like that,</i>

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:21.420
<i>or that they were artificially created.</i>

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.410
<i>That Birdy was born that way...</i>

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.290
That's enough!

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:33.130
That's a new time record.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:37.760
Time required to complete the <i>mission:</i> 1:00:48.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.460
Physical damage...

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.240
...is lower than last time as well.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.470
I did it!

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:50.110
Yes, you're truly talented.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:54.320
But never use that power on normal citizens.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:59.620
You'll just end up being treated like
a monster and feeling uncomfortable.

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:02.290
I know. At school the other day...

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:03.990
I don't care about school!

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.800
They can just scold Megius for that.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.830
What?

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.400
Come on, let's go eat something tasty!

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.800
Honestly...

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:21.740
Altans shouldn't be just
walking around in a place like this!

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:23.570
You damn brat!

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.580
You're the one who bumped into me!

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:27.680
What did you say?

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.590
You're pretty cheeky for an Altan!

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:34.580
Altans seriously reek!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.870
Sure he's a little kid, but he's still an Altan.

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:50.670
He might be a terrorist who
kills people like it's nothing!

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:52.110
Stop it!

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:58.150
What's with this Altan brat?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:01.150
Sh-She's an lxioran!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:04.140
Adults shouldn't be so mean to kids!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.890
Damn, we can't beat a monster like that!

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.460
Stay away from her!

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:17.170
Whoa, that's a lot of blood!

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.700
What's an "lxioran"?

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.040
I'm not really sure,

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.470
but we're tougher than Ulgarians and Garbelantans.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.710
Wow, that's major.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:25.510
Ow!

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.210
No, you have to tough it out until the bleeding stops.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:31.880
Oh, right, my name's Birdy. What's yours?

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:32.980
Nataru.

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.180
It's Nataru?!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.750
You know him?

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.090
He's on Earth.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:40.520
And... no, never mind.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:41.820
What is it?

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:45.090
I'm not sure if it's okay for me to tell you this,

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:50.370
but his dad used to be in Isdalta,
and he was helping the escapees.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:51.530
What?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:55.370
I know, come to my house! It's right nearby.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.210
Let's ask Violin to patch you up!

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.340
Violin?

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.170
Yep! Hurry!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.510
It's okay!

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.680
Here we go!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:12.890
Violin, I'll put the groceries over here.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.090
Thanks, Birdy.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:17.690
Were you on your way home from school?

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:19.730
I don't go to school.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.970
Why not? You should! It's fun!

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:26.800
You complain every day when you come home...

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:30.270
No, I'm friends with Kred and Miln now!

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:33.540
They picked on me at first,
but we get along now!

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.940
That's great, Birdy.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.310
And you made a new friend today, too.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:40.880
Yep! Nataru's my friend!

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:43.390
Nataru, have some coties before you go.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:47.060
Yeah! Violin's coties are the best!

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:50.460
They'll be done quick, so stick around, okay?

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:52.450
Thanks for the food!

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:06.440
Birdy, eat slowly! You're shocking Nataru.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.280
But it's so good!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.150
C'mon, you eat too, Nataru!

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:12.580
Okay.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.410
Thank you for the food.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:24.460
Don't worry about being polite.
Eat up, Nataru.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:25.860
Thank you.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.110
Later, Birdy!

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:40.310
See you tomorrow!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.500
Bye-bye!

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:52.040
Nataru?

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.290
Do you have some time?

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:04.670
Your dad?

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.500
Yeah, he said to bring you here.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.310
Do you hate it here?

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.980
Hey, what are those guys doing?!

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:21.480
They're playing a game of kamra.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:22.480
What's that?!

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.850
Dried manami.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:24.850
And that?!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.250
My apartment building.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.260
What's this?!

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.520
Stairs.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.390
And this place?!

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:30.490
It's where I live.

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:32.690
What's that?!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:33.680
It's...

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:37.090
Here, you go like this.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.400
Wow! What is it?

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:45.030
A kilk. It's a kid's toy that Dad made.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:49.840
It's so cool!

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:55.000
Dad!

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.960
Welcome home. You're early.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.460
Is that the man?

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:06.130
Yes, that's Nataru's father.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:09.970
U-Um, I'm Birdy Cephon. Hello.

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:11.270
Cephon?

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.400
So you <i>are</i> an lxioran...

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.270
You know about those, Dad?

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:19.240
It sounds like my son owes you for yesterday.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.710
l-It was nothing...

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:24.300
Come on. Let's go get some dinner.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:30.620
Oh, he's finally here.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.890
You're late, Dusk!

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.660
You guys are already tipsy?

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.260
Since we've got no jobs,
we've got plenty of time!

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.660
Finally, someone's come who can pay!

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.930
Once construction on the waterway
is done, I'll be unemployed.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:47.130
Cute girl. Is that Nataru's girlfriend?

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.240
I see he's a smooth
operator for someone his age!

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:57.450
My son was being harassed by Ulgarians...

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.280
and she saved him.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.820
What, that little girl?

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:03.290
From Ulgarians?

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:05.450
She's an lxioran.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:09.120
An lxioran?

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.360
Well, I guess it doesn't matter in this neighborhood.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:14.630
Yeah, not in a slum like this.

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.160
C'mere, pretty girl.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:18.000
Yeah, get over here!

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:23.640
What's wrong with you, Nataru?
Hurry up and find the pretty girl a seat!

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:28.280
That's right, the guy has to escort the girl!

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:30.810
What's wrong?

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.680
Why are you hesitating?

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:36.520
Well, usually even other Altans get
scared when they find out I'm lxioran...

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:39.390
These guys aren't narrow-minded like that.

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:41.620
Do you know what your job will be yet?

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:44.290
I go to the Federation Police Training Institute.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:45.530
Federation Police?

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:46.960
Now that's impressive!

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:50.960
If you distinguish yourself in the police,
you've got a shot at full citizenship!

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:01.640
Birdy, what do you think an lxioran's power is for?

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:06.050
Huh? Uh, stuff like helping your friends?

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:12.490
True. But you mustn't
become addicted to that power.

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:17.660
And you have to find the meaning
behind your being an lxioran.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:22.330
Every single person born into this world has a role.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:25.570
I do, you do, and Nataru does, too.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:31.440
But that role is <i>not</i> fated.
It's something you can find for yourself.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:35.440
You can forge your own future.

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:37.050
<i>Future...</i>

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:41.080
Value yourself...

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:45.080
For the sake of the future as well. Got it?

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.190
<i>Dusk...</i>

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.400
I'm sorry, Birdy.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.200
My dad was saying weird stuff.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:04.470
Naw, it was fun.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.470
Okay, see you.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:06.460
Yeah.

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:11.770
Hey...

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:22.260
Hey, can I come here again?
I like your neighborhood, and Dusk.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.590
And those drunk guys, too!

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.960
Sure, come anytime.

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:28.560
Okay!

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:30.760
See you later, then!

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:32.190
<i>And I get caught up in that battle too.</i>

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:36.190
<i>When Violin tries to help me, she...</i>

00:23:36.190 --> 00:23:39.180
<i>Violin, I still...!</i>
